---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { REPO } from '../data/site';
const entries = [
  { v: '0.1.2', date: 'October 2026 · release in progress', tag: 'Next', items: [
    'Update Moss from the panel: administrators get a notification and a short banner when a release is out, and Settings → Updates installs it, restarts Moss and reconnects the panel while game servers keep running.',
    'moss update installs the latest release (or --version) over the running binary with the installer\'s checks: checksum, cosign signature when cosign is installed, and a test run before the atomic swap. moss update --check only compares versions.',
    'Optional moss-update.path and moss-update.service units let the hardened systemd setup install updates from the panel; package-managed copies show the command to run instead. MOSS_UPDATE_CHECK=false turns the check off.',
    'One data folder wherever Moss starts: ~/.local/share/moss on Linux and ~/Library/Application Support/Moss/data on macOS. Data in an older ./moss-data, ~/moss/moss-data or ~/moss-data is still found and used.',
    'The install script and moss update ask before reinstalling the installed release, and the script warns about an older moss earlier on your PATH.',
    'moss doctor no longer creates a data folder where you run it or clears a running controller\'s temporary uploads.',
    'No database migrations and no new storage formats. Upgrading from v0.1.1 means running the install script once more.',
  ] },
  { v: '0.1.1', date: 'October 2026', tag: 'Latest', items: [
    'Sign-in works on a fresh install: the public sign-in settings are built into the binary, so moss serve needs no config file.',
    'Search Modrinth and CurseForge modpacks from New server → From modpack; pasting a link or uploading a pack still works.',
    'Accept the Minecraft EULA now or later: a server created without it will not start until it is accepted from the server page. Velocity no longer asks for it.',
    'Server memory is capped at the machine\'s RAM, a Setup tab keeps install and import logs, and imports get a drop zone and identify plugins and mods right away.',
    'Security: email confirmation is checked with Supabase itself, map links stop working within seconds of their holder losing access, games cannot swap Moss\'s console, log or config files for links to host files, and Forge and NeoForge installers are hash-checked.',
    'Reliability: per-user notification read state, backups that survive files changing mid-backup and never count failures toward keep N, a stop pressed during a start is honoured, and a failed modpack merge or restore cleans up after itself.',
    'One automatic database migration; no other storage format changes.',
  ] },
  { v: '0.1.0', date: 'October 2026', tag: 'First public release', items: [
    'One small Rust binary with the web panel built in: SQLite state, no Docker and no hosted backend, a first page load of about 34 KB, and servers that keep running when the controller restarts or is killed.',
    'Minecraft: Vanilla, Paper, Purpur, Folia, Fabric, Quilt, Forge 1.12.2+, NeoForge and Velocity from official metadata, with managed Temurin Java, crash detection with backoff, import, blueprints with share codes and a version upgrade assistant.',
    'Nineteen other games: Minecraft Bedrock, Terraria, Factorio and sixteen SteamCMD games from Valheim and Counter-Strike 2 to Rust, ARK, 7 Days to Die and Palworld, with RCON kick and ban, game mods, game updates and config editors.',
    'Mods and plugins from Modrinth, CurseForge and Hangar, checked against the real jars, with update-all, pinning, staged updates on a test copy, and modpack import, export, diff and pin.',
    'Checksummed backups with restore preview, staged and per-world restores, and remote destinations (a folder or any S3-compatible storage).',
    'Schedules in your time zone, event workflows, a notification inbox with Discord and webhook delivery, signed event webhooks and Web Push.',
    'Health findings with one-click fixes, long-term metrics, player analytics, shared allow and ban lists, live web maps and public status pages.',
    'Fourteen themes checked for WCAG AA contrast, a theme editor, saved views, a command palette and accessibility settings (text size up to 150%, strong focus ring, underlined links, wider spacing, reduced motion).',
    'Security: loopback by default, per-server permission checks on every call, invite-only sign-in with a setup token and optional MFA, hashed API tokens, confined files, hardened downloads and webhooks, and optional container isolation.',
    'Linux x86-64 and macOS (Apple silicon and Intel) downloads with an install script, a Homebrew formula and cosign-signed checksums.',
  ] },
];
---
<Base title="Changelog" description="What changed in each Moss release.">
  <div class="wrap page">
    <div class="prose">
      <span class="kicker">Changelog</span>
      <h1>Release notes</h1>
      <p class="lede">Full notes live on <a href={`${REPO}/releases`} rel="noopener">GitHub Releases</a>. This page keeps the highlights.</p>
      <div class="timeline">
        {entries.map((e) => (
          <article>
            <h2 style="margin:0 0 6px;padding:0">v{e.v} <span class="tag">{e.tag}</span></h2>
            <p style="margin:0 0 10px;color:var(--faint);font-size:14px">{e.date}</p>
            <ul>{e.items.map((i) => <li>{i}</li>)}</ul>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
